                    {
                        "sense_id": "bd2799fc-289c-3317-a678-e0e6de164369",
                        "entry_id": "e9759881-7f91-38f6-9c4e-b9d2c22bac25",
                        "glosses": [
                            "sprawa niepoważna, błaha, prosta"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbd7a1cb-a0d1-4878-8bea-57821ad86ab2",
                                "sense_id": "bd2799fc-289c-3317-a678-e0e6de164369",
                                "text": "Gestapo to dziecinada w porównaniu z NKWD."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0e0c9c53-8f34-39ab-be5f-8fe05521a8bc",
                        "entry_id": "e9759881-7f91-38f6-9c4e-b9d2c22bac25",
                        "glosses": [
                            "zachowanie niepoważne, dziecinny postępek"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "colloquial"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "efe1ec3f-e309-45a6-a603-dd0063db434d",
                                "sense_id": "0e0c9c53-8f34-39ab-be5f-8fe05521a8bc",
                                "text": "Zawsze jak mu się coś nie podoba, to się obraża, „zabiera zabawki” i idzie do domu. To przecież dziecinada."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.2\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "29f9a4ef-f90b-4270-aa2d-9846eb2da8ee",
                        "source_entry_id": "e9759881-7f91-38f6-9c4e-b9d2c22bac25",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd2799fc-289c-3317-a678-e0e6de164369",
                        "target_lang_word": "puerility",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "puerility",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3b6ba0b-6f0d-37a0-ab49-6d64f54d1691",
                                        "entry_id": "20fa9c4b-89d7-3b84-abbe-ba9ba42ce876",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state, quality, or condition of being childish or puerile."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9058a748-651a-4e99-a8d5-ff9d3ad052e2",
                                                "sense_id": "c3b6ba0b-6f0d-37a0-ab49-6d64f54d1691",
                                                "text": "This classification should have led to the discovery and study of remedies which act specifically upon the various textures and tissues of the body, such as the cellular, serous, mucous, parenchymatous, fibrous, gelatinous, &c., but it did not, except in the most imperfect manner—so imperfect, in fact, that most pathologists, despairing of finding such remedies, at one time sank into all the peurilities^([sic – meaning puerilities]) of the \"expectant mode\" of the French, or the nihilisms of the German."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "beff098a-a1a1-395d-9ab6-eea07274bbd2",
                                        "entry_id": "20fa9c4b-89d7-3b84-abbe-ba9ba42ce876",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That which is puerile or childish; especially, an expression which is insipid or silly."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0da36ef1-b3a7-4b37-9bb0-b80a978e0df0",
                                                "sense_id": "beff098a-a1a1-395d-9ab6-eea07274bbd2",
                                                "text": "You treat his opinions (though he never thrusts them on you) about \"the Church,\" and his duty, and the souls of his parishioners, with civil indifference, as much ado about nothing; and his rubrical eccentricities as puerilities."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b78041c-cdc6-4b05-ac69-91ecb9e26b71",
                        "source_entry_id": "e9759881-7f91-38f6-9c4e-b9d2c22bac25",
                        "source_sense_id": "bd2799fc-289c-3317-a678-e0e6de164369",
                        "target_lang_word": "childishness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "childishness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b7375113-060e-37ce-a351-77c142a70506",
                                        "entry_id": "2417c3a1-57ae-3898-b3c3-34a97130237f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or characteristic of being childish."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1c25650-e52b-31a3-91b0-3201c8419bba",
                                        "entry_id": "2417c3a1-57ae-3898-b3c3-34a97130237f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Childish behaviour."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7f6b5932-43dd-424e-835e-69b5d578e409",
                                                "sense_id": "d1c25650-e52b-31a3-91b0-3201c8419bba",
                                                "text": "Exorcism, unction, the sign of the cross, holy water, infant-communion, and many other childishnesses, were also called \"Apostolic institutions\" — not at first, but long after they were invented, to conceal their real origin […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "84ac27f3-7ab9-402e-8c66-15110f20f655",
                        "source_entry_id": "e9759881-7f91-38f6-9c4e-b9d2c22bac25",
                        "source_sense_id": "0e0c9c53-8f34-39ab-be5f-8fe05521a8bc",
                        "target_lang_word": "enfantillage",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "enfantillage",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fcc89828-f6aa-3ecc-aeb1-d7666324e942",
                                        "entry_id": "752ecb6e-7fab-3e75-8034-05c3f17d7215",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Manière d’agir ou de parler qui ne convient qu’à un enfant, en parlant des personnes qui ont passé l’enfance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3135c0d6-78ba-46ee-8e78-3e2819aaaa10",
                                                "sense_id": "fcc89828-f6aa-3ecc-aeb1-d7666324e942",
                                                "text": "À vingt-deux ans, les jeunes gens sont encore assez voisins de l’enfance pour se laisser aller à des enfantillages."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8405743a-73e3-4294-a4b9-b300e63cb4e6",
                                                "sense_id": "fcc89828-f6aa-3ecc-aeb1-d7666324e942",
                                                "text": "Je vous en prie, rompez là. C’est un enfantillage, et il faut que cela finisse au plus vite, sinon, nous serions profondément ridicules."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7ed525bb-8cac-492a-8d7c-eb72110b1f77",
                                                "sense_id": "fcc89828-f6aa-3ecc-aeb1-d7666324e942",
                                                "text": "On lira pour la première fois, chez un poète du VIIᵉ siècle, cet enfantillage charmant et qui semble du XIXᵉ :\n J’aime le nom de Leila. J’aime les noms qui ressemblent au sien."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ce31eb9-33c5-43e3-9ea5-c9653fad5ac8",
                                                "sense_id": "fcc89828-f6aa-3ecc-aeb1-d7666324e942",
                                                "text": "L’entêtement de Donald Trump à refuser d’admettre sa défaite confirme la thèse selon laquelle il se comporte comme un enfant de deux ans. Ce n’est pas de l’enfantillage."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
